{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And they dug.</b> Many say that the waters were blood-like in the hands of the Egyptian but turned clear in the hands of the Israelite. If so, why was this sign not written in the Torah? In my view, the plague of blood and the frogs and the lice encompassed both Egyptians and Hebrews, for after what is written we shall pursue, and these three did little harm. Only the plague of mixed beasts, which was severe, HaShem separated between the Egyptians and Israel; and likewise the plague of pestilence and hail, on account of their livestock — but not so with boils, and not with locusts, for they go forth from Egypt. And when the Egyptians dug, the Hebrews too dug."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:28.716632298Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}